        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ella Mary Leather, Ralph Vaughan Williams\n- Works: Twelve Traditional Carols from Herefordshire\n- Organizations: The Folklore Society\n- Topics: English folk-song, Tudor music, British music\n\nFacts:\n- Ralph Vaughan Williams was born on 12 October 1872 and died on 26 August 1958.\n- Ralph Vaughan Williams was an English composer.\n- Ralph Vaughan Williams was strongly influenced by Tudor music and English folk-song.\n- Ralph Vaughan Williams's output marked a decisive break in British music from its German-dominated 19th-century style.\n- Ella Mary Leather collaborated with Ralph Vaughan Williams on Twelve Traditional Carols from Herefordshire.\n- Ella Mary Leather also wrote notes for the journal of The Folklore Society.",
